<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Gaza</h1><p class="st-meta">1175 BCE – 332 BCE (approx.) · capital Gaza</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gaza, the southernmost Philistine city and the gateway between Egypt and Asia, a hub of the incense trade that resisted Alexander.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Gaza was the main Egyptian administrative base in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age">Late Bronze Age</a>. In the 12th century BCE <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/philistine-pentapolis">Philistines</a> settled there, and it became one of the cities of the Philistine Pentapolis, controlling the coastal road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings grew rich as the terminus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> carrying frankincense and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/myrrh">myrrh</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Bible</a> sets the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samson">Samson</a> in its temple of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagan">Dagon</a>. In 734 BCE King Hanunu fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> before Tiglath-Pileser III of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a>, who made Gaza a trading post.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> Gaza was a flourishing frontier city. In 332 BCE its commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batis">Batis</a> held out against Alexander of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a> for two months; the city was stormed and its people killed or enslaved.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1175 BCE – 332 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:36.32%;width:16.78%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1175 BCE – 332 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Gaza</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Hanunu, Sil-Bel</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Philistine religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Philistine, Canaanite</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Philistine Gaza</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-754&amp;focus=gaza" aria-label="Gaza on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5569 1030 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Gaza lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5889 1286L6092 1134M5889 1286L6140 1251M5889 1286L5548 987"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0M6140 1251h0M5548 987h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5889 1286h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5889 1286h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Gaza. <a href="/atlas?year=-754&amp;focus=gaza">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

